course: dictionary
lesson: 10818
title: Vegetables: a group word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A vegetable is a plant, or a part of a plant, that we eat, like a carrot, potato, cabbage or bean. Vegetables is a group word: it covers many different foods at once, so a problem may ask you to add up all the vegetables together.
explain: We can eat different parts of a plant. Roots are carrots, leaves are lettuce, stems are celery, flowers are broccoli and seeds are peas. «Wash fruit and vegetables before eating, because they may have dirt or chemicals on them.» Here the word covers all of these parts.
explain: Vegetable can also work as an describing word, as in vegetable oil, which is oil made from plants. Look at the words next to it to see which job it does. Informal words are short and friendly, so «veg» and «veggies» mean the same as vegetables.
fact: A vegetable is a plant or part of a plant that we eat.
fact: Carrots, potatoes, cabbages and beans are all vegetables.
fact: «Vegetable» can also describe something made from plants, as in «vegetable oil».
fact: «Veg» and «veggies» are informal words that mean vegetables.
fact: To a botanist a fruit is the part that holds the seeds, so tomatoes, cucumbers, peppers and pumpkins are fruits. In 1893 the US Supreme Court still ruled the tomato a vegetable for tax.
exercise: Which of these is a vegetable? | Biscuit | Lemonade | Chocolate cake | *Carrot
exercise: Lettuce is a vegetable. Which part of the plant do we eat? | *Leaves | Roots | Flowers | Seeds
exercise: «Vegetable oil» is oil made from what? | A sweet fruit juice | Milk | Fish | *Plants
test: Peas are a vegetable. Which part of the plant do we eat? | Leaves | Stems | Roots | *Seeds
test: Jack watches a video that says, «Vegetables are a scam.» What is the best thing to do? | Stop eating all plants at once | Believe it because it is on a video | *Check with a trusted source before you decide | Ignore fruit and vegetables for ever
exam: Which word is the informal short form of vegetables? | *veg | vet | vest | vex
